  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because the premise doesn't hold: `channel` on `OrderPlaced` is still read by another team's service.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest`:** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` parses `channel` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. A missing or unknown value makes ingestion reject the whole event with a `ContractViolationError`. `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `orders.channel` column. Its README (line 27) lists `channel` as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract.\n- **`billing-service`:** Its test helpers include `channel: \"web\"`. One test (`onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106`) passes `channel: undefined`, so billing probably doesn't depend on it.\n\nIf I removed `channel` from the event, analytics-ingest would reject every `OrderPlaced` event. That would stop the analytics pipeline until that team changed their code.\n\nInside orders-service, `channel` appears in these places:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: the `Order` and `NewOrder` types, `CHANNELS`, and validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: the event payload.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: request parsing.\n- Several tests.\n\nThe `POST /orders` example in `CLAUDE.md` and the README also includes it.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Remove it only from the order model and API, and keep it on the event.** That doesn't make sense, since the event is built from the order.\n2. **Coordinate with the analytics-ingest team first.** They would make `channel` optional or drop it, and then I'd remove it here.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now,** if you know analytics-ingest is already being changed. I'd also update the tests, `CLAUDE.md` and the README.",
